{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>Of David. To You, YHWH, I call.</b> David composed this psalm, or one of the singers [composed it] about him. He said: my Rock, facing those who go down into the pit." "<b>And the word תחרש</b> is from the root of silence [דומיה]. And they said: 'Do not be silent concerning your neighbor's harm' [to distinguish] between the accents, for the root is one."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 28, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:28:45.619470782Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}